WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:05.660
Hollywood has officially released another
big budget Robin Hood story, and you probably

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:06.380
didn't see it.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.100
What happened to make this reimagining stray
so far from the target?

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.760
And what could have been done differently?

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.320
Let's break down the real reasons Robin Hood
bombed at the box office.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.140
"Please tell me you got that."

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:22.080
Robin Hood attempted to revive a classic folk
tale with style and flair.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:27.180
With a cast including Taron Egerton, Jamie
Foxx, and Jamie Dornan, the movie tries to

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:31.180
tell a dark and gritty origin story along
the lines of Batman Begins.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:36.020
The movie's modern approach includes over
the top combat scenes, with automatic crossbows,

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.400
explosions, and super-stylish archery.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.220
Robin Hood himself is given a personality
upgrade, too.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.960
The outlaw has long been understood to be
a champion of the commoner, but now he's a

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.420
class-war-leading revolutionary with a puzzling
modern wardrobe.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.740
"This is a departure from your father's Robin
Hood.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.320
This one has a dope twist to it."

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:58.060
But all of these appeals to modern tastes
totally missed the mark with audiences, leaving

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:01.460
the movie falling flat on its face over the
long Thanksgiving weekend.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.119
No matter how you look at it, Robin Hood was
off to a disastrous start, only claiming the

00:01:07.119 --> 00:01:11.280
number seven spot at the domestic box office
in its first weekend of release.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:16.200
In the United States, it brought in just over
$14 million against a budget of reportedly

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.330
close to $100 million.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:23.229
With the movie having debuted on over 2,700
screens, that would seem to suggest a lot

00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:24.500
of empty theaters.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:29.440
Things seem equally dismal for Robin Hood
outside of the US, with the movie only bringing

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.500
in around $8.7 million from foreign markets.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.270
The performance made for total earnings of
about $23 million after the movie's first

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:41.700
weekend, enough for some commenters to call
it one of the biggest bombs of the year.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:47.220
Making things worse, that $100 million production
budget only covers costs before marketing,

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.260
meaning the movie is likely way more in the
red than the public will ever get to know.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.580
It's stunning how much money was sunk into
this movie since, despite all of its name

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.460
recognition, it was never a sure thing.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:58.660
"It's too dangerous"

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.780
"Ah but the danger's what makes it fun"

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:06.860
Though the 2018 Robin Hood movie was marketed
with the tagline "The legend you know, the

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.340
story you don't," that's little more than
wishful thinking.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.440
This story is extremely well-known.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:16.000
The Robin Hood folktale has been told on film
literally dozens of times, to the point where

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.530
even the most disengaged person could rattle
off the story's basics.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:23.060
"Robin Hood has a green hat, a bow and arrow,
and a loyal crew.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:25.140
He robs from the rich and gives to the poor.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:29.560
There's a friar named Tuck, a maid named Marian,
and a John who is little.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:30.560
They're all foxes."

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:31.440
You get the idea.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:35.940
How does a studio generate excitement for
a story that's been done to death over 700

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:36.540
years?

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.140
It's a good question, and one this movie clearly
failed to crack.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.590
Robin Hood's lukewarm reception can partially
be attributed to a lack of interesting star

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:46.080
power.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:51.000
Director Otto Bathurst reportedly waited a
year for lead actor Taron Egerton to become

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.720
available for this reimagining, being determined
to see him in the role.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:55.460
But why?

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:58.340
He explained his decision to the Courier Mail,
saying,

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:02.800
"I wanted to find someone who was accessible
and who seemed real, and Taron is that guy.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:06.820
He is incredibly charismatic and charming,
but he also has serious intensity."

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.940
"Taron's got a really fantastic kind of 'everyman'
about him.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:12.780
Serving up the emotional drama and then also
the fun"

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:17.340
Despite a relatively solid critical track
record, Egerton has never proven himself to

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:21.880
be a huge draw in a lead role, at least outside
of the success of the star-studded Kingsman

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:22.380
movies.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:26.280
Despite technically being the protagonist
of that series, Egerton's role has generally

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.260
been but one small part of a more famous ensemble.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:34.319
Even with a capable assist from Jamie Foxx
and others, it's possible that this cast just

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.700
wasn't enough of a draw for the well-worn
material.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:41.780
If Robin Hood had come out during a barren
weekend in January, it might have stood a

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:42.280
chance.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:46.840
Instead, it made its debut during one of the
most packed release windows of the whole year,

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:47.640
and got trampled.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.880
Coming in at number one over the long Thanksgiving
weekend was Ralph Breaks the Internet, the

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:56.040
Wreck-It Ralph sequel that stomped its competition
with the second-best Thanksgiving opening

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:56.540
ever.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:02.600
The movie also debuted below Creed II, The
Grinch, Fantastic Beasts 2, and Bohemian Rhapsody.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:07.480
It even performed worse than the modestly-budgeted
Mark Wahlberg comedy Instant Family, which

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:11.540
was holding onto sixth place in its second
week during Robin Hood's rollout.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:15.660
Apparently, all six of these movies are more
compelling options for holiday moviegoers,

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:20.700
once again suggesting that audiences really
don't care about the Robin Hood story anymore.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.240
All of these factors could have been overcome
if Robin Hood had turned out to be an awesome

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:25.740
movie.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:30.600
But it unfortunately debuted to a dismal reception
from critics and audiences alike.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:36.490
Rotten Tomatoes, counting roughly 100 reviews,
initially tallied a 13% approval rating for

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:41.050
the movie, marking it one of the worst-received
adaptations of the Robin Hood story yet.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:45.509
It also got a middling B Cinemascore, which
tends not to translate into positive word

00:04:45.509 --> 00:04:46.000
of mouth.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.439
On the other hand, between its weird costumes
and other strange anachronisms, there's a

00:04:50.439 --> 00:04:53.240
lot about Robin Hood that audiences have found
amusing.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:58.379
Richard Roeper, writing for the Chicago Sun-Times,
even said that the film is "legitimately funny."

00:04:58.379 --> 00:05:02.639
It has the makings of a movie that's so off-base
and over-the-top that it actually becomes

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:03.140
good.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.460
But that kind of reputation usually isn't
enough to make the hundred million dollars

00:05:07.469 --> 00:05:09.229
this movie desperately needs.

00:05:09.229 --> 00:05:13.111
While Robin Hood may have enough of a spark
of madness to be kind of entertaining, it

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.800
doesn't seem to be working on audiences in
the way its producers intended.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:21.059
Despite ending with a sequel tease, it seems
doubtful at this point that the tale will

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:21.580
continue.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:25.820
Hopefully the next people who try and make
a movie out of Robin Hood take the hint.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:27.140
We know this story already.

00:05:27.389 --> 00:05:29.000
Maybe it's just time for something new.

